      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KING KASEY (3) settled handy then found the lead and closed the race off too well to take out a 1785m race at Stawell last start, putting an impressive 11 metres on his nearest rival. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Meets a similar line up so he can certainly win again. JOE GOT ROLLED (1) has been in the placings two times from as many runs this campaign. Went well again last time over 2200m at Ballarat, finishing second and 5 metres from the winner. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Taking on a better line-up this time but she good enough to play a major role. AMALFI NZ (11) is also high on the list of contenders despite a tough draw. Best form measures up favourably in this line-up so just needs a bit of luck to go his way. OCEAN AVENUE (7) must be considered after he finished runner-up over 2240m at Melton two-and-a-half weeks ago.",
